- Story & Context: Elara, the lead pianist, stands in the center of the ring confessing her betrayal to the dark tunnels, her hands raw from hammering out a discordant boogie-woogie on keys that feel like frozen glass. The incident escalated when the room's gravity began to warp, pulling her sheet music toward the ceiling in a spiral of charred parchment. "My skin is just the leaden sleeve that keeps the lightning in."
